cmu-voice-intro-title = Voice Chat
cmu-voice-intro-heading = This server has proximity voice chat.
cmu-voice-intro-body = Your voice comes from your character: players nearby hear you, louder the closer they are, and walls muffle you. It runs in a browser tab that stays open while you play.
cmu-voice-intro-keys-heading = Talking
cmu-voice-intro-keys = Voice is push-to-talk only.
    • Hold [bold]{$ptt}[/bold] to talk to people around you.
    • Hold [bold]{$radio}[/bold] to talk on your headset radio. You'll hear a click as it keys up.
    • Press [bold]{$cycle}[/bold] to switch radio channel, or [bold]shift-click your headset[/bold] to pick your channel and mute the ones you don't want to hear.
cmu-voice-intro-tips-heading = Good to know
cmu-voice-intro-tips = • The list in the bottom-right shows who you're hearing and how: radio channel, PA, shouting or whispering.
    • Whisper and only people right next to you hear it; shout and it carries further.
    • Gas masks and helmets muffle your voice. Voice reaches other floors only through openings.
    • Command staff can make live voice announcements from overwatch and communications consoles.
    • Only humans can use voice chat. Ghosts can listen but can't speak.
cmu-voice-intro-open = Open voice chat
cmu-voice-intro-open-desc = Opens the voice chat page in your browser. Allow your microphone and keep the tab open.
cmu-voice-intro-close = Not now
